# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the keys you have.
# Every key here is optional. If a key is missing, the feature it powers
# is disabled in the UI with a clear "unavailable" message instead of
# crashing or silently failing. Nothing in this file is a real secret.

# --- Supabase (auth, database, storage) ---
# Required for accounts and backing detectors up off this machine. Without
# these the app still works: detectors live in the browser's IndexedDB and the
# account control simply isn't shown.
#
# Public and safe to expose in the browser bundle -- what separates one
# account's photos from another is Row Level Security, not secrecy of this key.
#
# NOTE: anything NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUILD time, not read at runtime.
# Adding these in Vercel does nothing until a new build runs, and "Redeploy" on
# an existing deployment rebuilds THAT commit -- push, or redeploy the latest.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Anthropic (AI-assisted labeling) ---
# Powers the "Claude proposes a label" step when reviewing uploaded examples.
# Without this, the wizard falls back to fully manual labeling.
#
# This spends YOUR key, so the route requires a signed-in account and meters
# each one to 600 photos a month (supabase/migrations/0007_label_allowance.sql).
# It therefore needs the Supabase keys above as well: without them the step is
# switched off rather than left open to anyone who finds the endpoint.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Email (the "send an email" trigger action) ---
# Set ONE of these. The variable name selects the provider, because the two
# services use different endpoints, auth headers and body shapes -- a Brevo key
# in RESEND_API_KEY authenticates against nothing. Without either, the email
# action is disabled in the trigger picker with a note saying why.
RESEND_API_KEY=
BREVO_API_KEY=
# Sender address. Must be one your provider has verified, or sending fails.
EMAIL_FROM=
